x-scheme-handler/claude-cli=claude-code-url-handler.desktop
x-scheme-handler/mailto=org.mozilla.Thunderbird.desktop
# Text goes to Zed. Omarchy's /usr/share/applications/mimeapps.list points the
# first block below at nvim.desktop, and this file is the user layer that
# overrides it. Two resolvers read this file and they differ. gio (Nautilus,
# GTK) types files by shared-mime-info glob and walks the type's ancestry, so
# text/plain alone would catch json, python and friends there, but a registered
# app for a specific type beats the parent's default, which is why
# text/markdown (omawrite) and xml (chrome) are spelled out. xdg-open on
# Hyprland takes xdg-utils' generic path: it types files with libmagic (`file
# --mime-type`), whose names differ from freedesktop's (text/x-script.python,
# text/x-shellscript), and it does NOT walk ancestry, so an unlisted type falls
# through to $BROWSER. Hence the second block (freedesktop names, for gio and
# for future apps that register them) and the third (libmagic names, for
# xdg-open). text/html here is the *file* association only; http/https URLs
# are x-scheme-handler entries above and still go to the browser. Deliberately
# not Zed: the documents, playlists, certificates and svg that are technically
# text/plain subclasses but have a real viewer registered.
text/plain=dev.zed.Zed.desktop
text/english=dev.zed.Zed.desktop
text/markdown=dev.zed.Zed.desktop
text/csv=dev.zed.Zed.desktop
